[{:db/id "q-109021/selection/118c13ea6e25b4401702655c0d5028ac312cb23c578b1d6dd82cbe55c0be2e7f" :answer/id #uuid "61090dbc-9ec4-5a3c-8b6c-8decc70cf6a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4{x}^{3}}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109021/selection/32ce4c1478eb454b31417c1b0e43bc6209413ce7d000403471be5e213d315bec" :answer/id #uuid "6a259432-1b1e-5ebb-b9ae-c48fa783330e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{3}}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109021/selection/da159ae369162e2895939f6a28d63fe202dfe670f7f7673638546872418b0246" :answer/id #uuid "32af292a-783e-5ab6-8c9b-03fbd575cebb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109021/selection/04fa0ca9b5eba7d8b284177888e332d88a4ffcb925f249014f04031a6237f508" :answer/id #uuid "e2428fd3-c0b5-51a3-8140-ab5648378d54" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4{x}^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109021/selection/e5f83e74480eeba77b0d9c7c6ab38fc457f5dffe0dfdfca3a81d5606443223f2" :answer/id #uuid "88fb7b17-1892-534e-983a-5947c47d555a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109021/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "acb9739b-df49-5f18-bb5b-0417ac37adcd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-109021/selection/32ce4c1478eb454b31417c1b0e43bc6209413ce7d000403471be5e213d315bec" :answer-field/choices ["q-109021/selection/118c13ea6e25b4401702655c0d5028ac312cb23c578b1d6dd82cbe55c0be2e7f" "q-109021/selection/32ce4c1478eb454b31417c1b0e43bc6209413ce7d000403471be5e213d315bec" "q-109021/selection/da159ae369162e2895939f6a28d63fe202dfe670f7f7673638546872418b0246" "q-109021/selection/04fa0ca9b5eba7d8b284177888e332d88a4ffcb925f249014f04031a6237f508" "q-109021/selection/e5f83e74480eeba77b0d9c7c6ab38fc457f5dffe0dfdfca3a81d5606443223f2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-109021" :question/id #uuid "3bbe7f28-efd3-56e9-a3e7-84fe99064a40" :question/math-academy-id "q-109021" :question/problem "The substitution $z={y}^{m}$ for some real number $m$ transforms the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+\\frac{y}{x}={x}^{3}{y}^{3/4}\n$$\n\ninto an equation of the form ${z}^{′}(x)+P(x)z(x)=Q(x).$ What is the function $Q(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that our equation is an instance of the Bernoulli differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+p(x)y=q(x){y}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)=\\frac{1}{x},\\,q(x)={x}^{3},\\,n=\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we divide the differential equation by ${y}^{3/4},$ and we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{-3/4}\\frac{dy}{dx}+\\frac{{y}^{1/4}}{x}={x}^{3}.\\,\\,(∗)\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz={y}^{1-n}={y}^{1/4}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{4}{y}^{-3/4}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,{y}^{-3/4}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=4\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, equation $(∗)$ can be written as a linear equation in $z(x)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n4\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{x}\\,z={x}^{3}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the above equation in standard form, which gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{4x}\\,z=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $Q(x)=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{4}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-109021/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5dc2192f-24a4-5160-844c-4d17096779e5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-109021"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-109024/selection/232a5dada091313e16984e74d3bb5db444374b46d43b46399f9b4745bb7bd053" :answer/id #uuid "31df7db3-f90e-57fa-9036-59679e679851" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109024/selection/0e4ac7b881081f480033aa7f9682beb7bda4c107781e4b5ad95a360235a699cf" :answer/id #uuid "11354af7-b2c7-520f-95c1-717104e7bedf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3{x}^{5}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109024/selection/7e03d2c00248fa364f3800ef733109c9125806465539f984754c4524194916fc" :answer/id #uuid "0bd19702-9c54-5140-ba6b-1087862af8ef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{5}}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109024/selection/eabd2bb9ff2e8e097eca21043daf2846d321bc8307d47abdc5eecea8e772aaa8" :answer/id #uuid "8638cc8e-5c91-5ab9-ba33-82dd1153cc34" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3x}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109024/selection/4e4d282eb47c56c6478b3beabc1cb7ab8078464f1b9c2906dce4c3484400f531" :answer/id #uuid "0623ed2a-bdd6-5cae-b2c5-e807cdf30235" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2x}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109024/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6b3de7a7-0d97-5379-80f9-4e237ee41ece" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-109024/selection/4e4d282eb47c56c6478b3beabc1cb7ab8078464f1b9c2906dce4c3484400f531" :answer-field/choices ["q-109024/selection/232a5dada091313e16984e74d3bb5db444374b46d43b46399f9b4745bb7bd053" "q-109024/selection/0e4ac7b881081f480033aa7f9682beb7bda4c107781e4b5ad95a360235a699cf" "q-109024/selection/7e03d2c00248fa364f3800ef733109c9125806465539f984754c4524194916fc" "q-109024/selection/eabd2bb9ff2e8e097eca21043daf2846d321bc8307d47abdc5eecea8e772aaa8" "q-109024/selection/4e4d282eb47c56c6478b3beabc1cb7ab8078464f1b9c2906dce4c3484400f531"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-109024" :question/id #uuid "023ae6da-320c-5d9f-893c-3cafd754c018" :question/math-academy-id "q-109024" :question/problem "The substitution $z={y}^{m}$ for some real number $m$ transforms the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}-xy=\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{y}}{{x}^{5}}\n$$\n\ninto an equation of the form ${z}^{′}(x)+P(x)z(x)=Q(x).$ What is the function $P(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that our equation is an instance of the Bernoulli differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+p(x)y=q(x){y}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)=-x,\\,q(x)={x}^{-5},\\,n=\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we divide the differential equation by ${y}^{1/3},$ and we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{-1/3}\\frac{dy}{dx}-x{y}^{2/3}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{5}}.\\,\\,(∗)\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz={y}^{1-n}={y}^{2/3}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2}{3}{y}^{-1/3}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,{y}^{-1/3}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3}{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, equation $(∗)$ can be written as a linear equation in $z(x)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-x\\,z=\\frac{1}{{x}^{5}}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the above equation in standard form, which gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{2x}{3}\\,z=\\frac{2}{3{x}^{5}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=-\\frac{2x}{3}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-109024/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5dc2192f-24a4-5160-844c-4d17096779e5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-109024"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-109027/selection/cd3c9c41f2d272b63d7fe8a39d04333b8036dad0f858fe36097101d8ccf1b03e" :answer/id #uuid "cb18262f-5203-5e13-acf6-8c9af8fb1ef5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[5]{\\frac{C{e}^{x}-1}{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109027/selection/0af1a04172492dd8f600b0f26fd638d55f9bb0d780bfc7499f02e0f9a0cde46f" :answer/id #uuid "e26eb2a3-f820-5d12-b6dd-71854a0f9967" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[5]{\\frac{C-{e}^{5{x}^{3}}}{{x}^{2}}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109027/selection/cafeded079853e151543e45a18afc67e2533c21e1062053d0420920bdb1045aa" :answer/id #uuid "6b5c237e-1202-5915-8012-04fdd3a5e0e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{C-{e}^{3{x}^{2}}}{x}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109027/selection/eb524df6a1abcbf6bbecdd77849b1848e0737152818cbc22f3c64e3503b56fbe" :answer/id #uuid "b4d54925-04a5-52ae-8425-88472a7940b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[5]{\\frac{C{e}^{5{x}^{3}}-1}{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109027/selection/52a70370738d51a61508be3be7a5c59c89bc6f0d88c7ec1eb8db47167abae02d" :answer/id #uuid "2b08c91a-aca9-5016-8503-b32cc4bb1e66" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{C{e}^{3{x}^{2}}-1}{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109027/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "69e4b3a8-2ec3-5c49-a6cd-2f7311b25459" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-109027/selection/eb524df6a1abcbf6bbecdd77849b1848e0737152818cbc22f3c64e3503b56fbe" :answer-field/choices ["q-109027/selection/cd3c9c41f2d272b63d7fe8a39d04333b8036dad0f858fe36097101d8ccf1b03e" "q-109027/selection/0af1a04172492dd8f600b0f26fd638d55f9bb0d780bfc7499f02e0f9a0cde46f" "q-109027/selection/cafeded079853e151543e45a18afc67e2533c21e1062053d0420920bdb1045aa" "q-109027/selection/eb524df6a1abcbf6bbecdd77849b1848e0737152818cbc22f3c64e3503b56fbe" "q-109027/selection/52a70370738d51a61508be3be7a5c59c89bc6f0d88c7ec1eb8db47167abae02d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-109027" :question/id #uuid "90997a63-8b0a-5ca6-9670-b13bb0d8de17" :question/math-academy-id "q-109027" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3{x}^{2}y={x}^{2}{y}^{-4}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that our equation is an instance of the Bernoulli differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+p(x)y=q(x){y}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)=-3{x}^{2},\\,q(x)={x}^{2},\\,n=-4.\n$$\n\nFirst, we multiply the differential equation by ${y}^{4},$ and we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{4}\\frac{dy}{dx}-3{x}^{2}{y}^{5}={x}^{2}.\\,\\,(∗)\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz={y}^{1-n}={y}^{5}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=5{y}^{4}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,{y}^{4}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{5}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z(x)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{5}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-3{x}^{2}z={x}^{2}\n$$\n\nThis differential equation is linear, so we can use the method of integrating factors. But first, we write the above equation in standard form:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-15{x}^{2}z=5{x}^{2}\n$$\n\nThe above equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x)=-15{x}^{2},\\,Q(x)=5{x}^{2}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute an integrating factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (-15{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{-5{x}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the standard form equation by $I(x)={e}^{-5{x}^{3}}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-5{x}^{3}}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-15{x}^{2}z) & ={e}^{-5{x}^{3}}\\cdot (5{x}^{2}) \\\\ {e}^{-5{x}^{3}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-15{x}^{2}z{e}^{-5{x}^{3}} & =5{x}^{2}{e}^{-5{x}^{3}} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(z{e}^{-5{x}^{3}}) & =5{x}^{2}{e}^{-5{x}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(z{e}^{-5{x}^{3}})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 5{x}^{2}{e}^{-5{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ z{e}^{-5{x}^{3}} & =-\\frac{{e}^{-5{x}^{3}}}{3}+{C}_{1} \\\\ z & =\\frac{C{e}^{5{x}^{3}}-1}{3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=3{C}_{1}.$\n\nFinally, we determine $y(x)$ by writing $z={y}^{5}.$ This results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{5}=\\frac{C{e}^{5{x}^{3}}-1}{3}\\,⇒\\,y=\\sqrt[5]{\\frac{C{e}^{5{x}^{3}}-1}{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-109027/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "17061f4e-da7c-58f9-90b4-47bdc21505da"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-109027"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-109028/selection/cec0c05ad2cb0ceb3dd8f5d99453ebaced64d1a82144dd362d9cbbae602ce8e4" :answer/id #uuid "c26b94f6-7d3f-5f6e-a2cd-3fe2d88b4bf4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{2x+1}{C-{e}^{2x}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109028/selection/d419967b38eecdf5b6783860ebff2e5475a724d3565d1d1f9ca139710327e3a1" :answer/id #uuid "ced8eb65-de8c-580d-9481-5a07bfd6fd04" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{2}{C{e}^{x}-2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109028/selection/a58254a437250b2f5464cfc3591a43a31125cf2a73a872420da3f63d1bc90fbd" :answer/id #uuid "08c1b73a-ddb0-5185-a9d2-4295e6b3ab74" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{C{e}^{2x}-2x-1}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109028/selection/a73116d5f3222a04c0ddc4e9853d204d239bb1628758e5bdf64a6cd33107aa67" :answer/id #uuid "b312561b-17a7-5f1b-9e25-632d8ccc99c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{C{e}^{x}-1}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109028/selection/b19f738cb8fc741417667131308807c0fd3626bba61aa4516087624302e57ced" :answer/id #uuid "55e0d93a-8572-52e1-a086-959899b473e3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{2x}{C+{e}^{2x}}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109028/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "581e3af7-db14-5b36-b226-a78708939c61" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-109028/selection/a58254a437250b2f5464cfc3591a43a31125cf2a73a872420da3f63d1bc90fbd" :answer-field/choices ["q-109028/selection/cec0c05ad2cb0ceb3dd8f5d99453ebaced64d1a82144dd362d9cbbae602ce8e4" "q-109028/selection/d419967b38eecdf5b6783860ebff2e5475a724d3565d1d1f9ca139710327e3a1" "q-109028/selection/a58254a437250b2f5464cfc3591a43a31125cf2a73a872420da3f63d1bc90fbd" "q-109028/selection/a73116d5f3222a04c0ddc4e9853d204d239bb1628758e5bdf64a6cd33107aa67" "q-109028/selection/b19f738cb8fc741417667131308807c0fd3626bba61aa4516087624302e57ced"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-109028" :question/id #uuid "21b39c4d-cfb3-59e7-bfe5-8b7a15dc1142" :question/math-academy-id "q-109028" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+y=-x{y}^{3}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that our equation is an instance of the Bernoulli differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+p(x)y=q(x){y}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)=1,\\,q(x)=-x,\\,n=3.\n$$\n\nFirst, we divide the differential equation by ${y}^{3},$ and we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{-3}\\frac{dy}{dx}+{y}^{-2}=-x.\\,\\,(∗)\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz={y}^{1-n}={y}^{-2}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=-2{y}^{-3}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,{y}^{-3}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z(x)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n-\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+z=-x\n$$\n\nThis differential equation is linear, so we can use the method of integrating factors. But first, we write the above equation in standard form:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-2z=2x\n$$\n\nThe above equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x)=-2,\\,Q(x)=2x\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute an integrating factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (-2)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{-2x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the standard form equation by $I(x)={e}^{-2x}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-2x}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-2z) & ={e}^{-2x}\\cdot (2x) \\\\ {e}^{-2x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-2z{e}^{-2x} & =2x{e}^{-2x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(z{e}^{-2x}) & =2x{e}^{-2x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(z{e}^{-2x})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 2x{e}^{-2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ z{e}^{-2x} & =-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-2x}(2x+1)+{C}_{1} \\\\ z & =\\frac{C{e}^{2x}-2x-1}{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=2{C}_{1}.$\n\nFinally, we determine $y(x)$ by writing $z={y}^{-2}.$ This results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{-2}=\\frac{C{e}^{2x}-2x-1}{2}\\,⇒\\,y=\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{C{e}^{2x}-2x-1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-109028/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "17061f4e-da7c-58f9-90b4-47bdc21505da"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-109028"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-109154/selection/461a56c437def93c3969474b02044cad03ec3865dbc61d4b169d1669b3092652" :answer/id #uuid "e9b16c4a-1802-5e22-9ce7-ae7b641fb6c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{5x}{C-2{x}^{5/2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109154/selection/ab06742b724332c0ea6737dbf6db0395708fa0462690fcbc0fc22b5cf22aa895" :answer/id #uuid "0fe0dfa2-f184-50ee-ae9d-bd46cd9ee6a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{x}{C+{x}^{5/2}}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109154/selection/33f31315c207be6f0a7885bce59c9481fcb70b7fd996232fb4c178edb057a5b5" :answer/id #uuid "9f7699e8-a6fa-5ae7-bd4a-9cb54c850ce0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{5x}{C+{x}^{3/2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109154/selection/5f3363a81539edf16de86a396960f847cfa267d9028062a94fada203880b9cfd" :answer/id #uuid "6fd95274-821b-5b36-a4b3-a6b7d28a48db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={(\\frac{2x}{C-{x}^{3/2}})}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109154/selection/0e48d6abe0998fffb6b9c3afcd4637ad24b92df81ca64f58bd3de7b3ea505d00" :answer/id #uuid "04841c1a-60c3-57db-91b5-dcbeab6a0fef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{C-5{x}^{5/2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109154/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1f367fc4-b717-5b6e-81f2-788d821286e9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-109154/selection/461a56c437def93c3969474b02044cad03ec3865dbc61d4b169d1669b3092652" :answer-field/choices ["q-109154/selection/461a56c437def93c3969474b02044cad03ec3865dbc61d4b169d1669b3092652" "q-109154/selection/ab06742b724332c0ea6737dbf6db0395708fa0462690fcbc0fc22b5cf22aa895" "q-109154/selection/33f31315c207be6f0a7885bce59c9481fcb70b7fd996232fb4c178edb057a5b5" "q-109154/selection/5f3363a81539edf16de86a396960f847cfa267d9028062a94fada203880b9cfd" "q-109154/selection/0e48d6abe0998fffb6b9c3afcd4637ad24b92df81ca64f58bd3de7b3ea505d00"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-109154" :question/id #uuid "692fec97-1d1e-5270-a23f-3b8552e51e1f" :question/math-academy-id "q-109154" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{y}{x}=\\sqrt{x}\\,{y}^{2}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that our equation is an instance of the Bernoulli differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+p(x)y=q(x){y}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)=-\\frac{1}{x},\\,q(x)=\\sqrt{x},\\,n=2.\n$$\n\nFirst, we divide the differential equation by ${y}^{2},$ and we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{-2}\\frac{dy}{dx}-\\frac{1}{x}{y}^{-1}=\\sqrt{x}.\\,\\,(∗)\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz={y}^{1-n}={y}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=-{y}^{-2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,{y}^{-2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z(x)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n-\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{1}{x}z=\\sqrt{x}\n$$\n\nThis differential equation is linear, so we can use the method of integrating factors. But first, we write the above equation in standard form:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{x}z=-\\sqrt{x}\n$$\n\nThe above equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x)=\\frac{1}{x},\\,Q(x)=-\\sqrt{x}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute an integrating factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (1/x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the standard form equation by $I(x)=x$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{x}z) & =x\\cdot (-\\sqrt{x}) \\\\ x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+z & =-x\\sqrt{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(xz) & =-{x}^{3/2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(xz)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int -{x}^{3/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ xz & =-\\frac{2{x}^{5/2}}{5}+{C}_{1} \\\\ z & =\\frac{C-2{x}^{5/2}}{5x},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=5{C}_{1}.$\n\nFinally, we determine $y(x)$ by writing $z={y}^{-1}.$ This results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{-1}=\\frac{C-2{x}^{5/2}}{5x}\\,⇒\\,y=\\frac{5x}{C-2{x}^{5/2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-109154/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "17061f4e-da7c-58f9-90b4-47bdc21505da"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-109154"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
